{"availability":"available","full":"judegomila/OnCo","name":"OnCo","description":"OnCo: total information dominance on cancer. A public, cited knowledge graph of oncology with a website, JSON API, MCP server and CLI: one page per cancer, treatment, target, trial, institution, person and idea.","category":"Developer tools","language":"TypeScript","stars":194,"forks":31,"created":"2026-09-05T01:41:54Z","updated":"2026-10-04T05:02:35Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://onco.cc","topics":["cancer","cli","clinical-trials","knowledge-graph","mcp","nextjs","oncology","open-data","precision-medicine","public-health"],"demo":null,"color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-04T06:51:33.587Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-04T06:51:33.587Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-04T06:51:33.587Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-03T21:19:13.823Z","stars":194,"forks":31},{"at":"2026-10-04T06:51:33.587Z","stars":194,"forks":31}],"technologies":["React","Next.js"],"lastDemoCheckedAt":"2026-10-04T06:12:35.448Z","overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["OnCo is an open repository for cancer. The whole corpus, every page, source, drawing, translation and script, is in this repository under an open licence (CC BY-NC 4.0 for the data, MIT for the code), built in public, corrected through issues and pull requests, and free for patients, clinicians, researchers, companies and AI agents to read and reuse. If you know something the site does not, open an issue or a pull request: the gate runs the same checks on every contribution.","OnCo is a public, cited knowledge graph of oncology, aiming at total information dominance on cancer: every cancer, front, technology, target, biomarker readout, treatment and test, company, institution, person, pathway, trial, key paper, journal, pairing, roadmap, bottleneck and idea, one page each, with a plain-English TL;DR before the technical layer and links in every direction. Readers start in a Global view and pick their country, so \"approved\" means their regulator's verdict. It exists so that a patient, a carer, a clinician, a scientist, an investor or a policymaker can walk from any…","The website is one surface. The same corpus ships as:"],"features":["the site ( tables with filters, tooltips on every technical term, molecule and target renderings, animated schematics, a graph explorer, Ask OnCo question answering, a living-with-cancer area (side effects, symptoms,…","a static JSON API under with CORS, per-entity Markdown context files for language models, Atom feeds and RDF triples;","an MCP server and a command-line tool (packages/), so agents and scripts can search, fetch, compare and ask over the corpus;","browser WebMCP tools for read-only record search and lookup in supporting browsers (implementation and testing);","eight interface languages with translated TL;DRs where a translation exists."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/judegomila/OnCo/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"f060aead9cfdd392251200593534786bc79062da14c2df178b5b00131315c134","extractedAt":"2026-10-03T06:15:01.336Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-04T06:12:35.446Z","overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-04T05:02:35Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"OnCo is an open repository for cancer. The whole corpus, every page, source, drawing, translation and script, is in this repository under an open licence (CC BY-NC 4.0 for the data, MIT for the code), built in public, corrected through issues and pull requests, and free for patients, clinicians, researchers, companies and AI agents to read and reuse. If you know something the site does not, open an issue or a pull request: the gate runs the same checks on every contribution.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/judegomila/OnCo/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"f060aead9cfdd392251200593534786bc79062da14c2df178b5b00131315c134","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/judegomila/OnCo/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-04T06:12:35.446Z"}